{"id": "q24_comp_fractional_vs_01_knapsack", "query": "What is the difference between fractional knapsack and 0/1 knapsack?", "category": "comparison", "is_negative": false, "expected_status": "partially_answered", "expected_youtube_ids": ["F_DDzYnxO14"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["70f39599-429d-563d-8ce4-7d380b64a0f9"], "latency_ms": 18055.7, "error": null, "actual_status": "partially_answered", "status_match": 1, "answer": "In the lecture the fractional knapsack problem is described as one where you are allowed to take a part of an item \u2013 you can pick fractional weights of an item to fill the knapsack (e.g., \u201cit is not necessary that you take up this entire value and take up this entire weight you can take a part of it\u201d [S2]; \u201cour knapsack does allow fractional elements to be picked\u201d [S4]). The lecture does not discuss the 0/1 knapsack variant, which would require each item to be taken either completely or not at all. Therefore, the difference that the 0/1 knapsack disallows fractions cannot be confirmed from the provided transcript.", "citations_count": 2, "citation_yts": ["F_DDzYnxO14", "F_DDzYnxO14"], "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F_DDzYnxO14&t=0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F_DDzYnxO14&t=437"], "citation_sources": ["S2", "S4"], "citations_valid": 1, "video_aligned": 1}
