{"id": "q_part_01_knapsack_greedy_and_dp", "query": "Explain the fractional knapsack greedy algorithm and also provide the 2D dynamic programming recurrence relation for 0/1 knapsack.", "category": "partially_supported", "is_negative": false, "expected_status": "partially_answered", "expected_youtube_ids": ["F_DDzYnxO14"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["9133f4ee-7f12-5c24-a99e-081ef4e62c20", "f9d5d93f-ed94-53e8-9c10-540f906aac4f"], "latency_ms": 16040.3, "error": null, "actual_status": "partially_answered", "status_match": 1, "answer": "The lecture explains the greedy solution for the fractional knapsack problem as follows: 1. Compute value-per-weight ratio. 2. Sort items descending. 3. Take whole items while capacity permits. 4. Take fraction of next item to fill remaining capacity. The lecture does not cover the 2D dynamic programming recurrence relation for 0/1 knapsack.", "citations_count": 3, "citation_yts": ["F_DDzYnxO14"], "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F_DDzYnxO14&t=87", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F_DDzYnxO14&t=351", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F_DDzYnxO14&t=437"], "citation_sources": ["S1", "S3", "S4"], "citations_valid": 1, "video_aligned": 1}
{"id": "q_part_02_platforms_and_toposort", "query": "How do you calculate the minimum number of railway platforms using arrival and departure times, and how does Kahn algorithm perform topological sorting?", "category": "partially_supported", "is_negative": false, "expected_status": "partially_answered", "expected_youtube_ids": ["dxVcMDI7vyI"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["0399a0f1-29d1-5900-9926-22c10ca4cffc", "7a238c5b-eadf-5917-9ad5-9401f10961f0"], "latency_ms": 24909.1, "error": null, "actual_status": "partially_answered", "status_match": 1, "answer": "Minimum number of railway platforms: 1. Sort arrival and departure times separately. 2. Use two pointers. 3. If arrival <= departure, increment platforms and advance arrival pointer; else decrement and advance departure. 4. Track max platforms. Kahn's algorithm for topological sorting is not discussed in the lecture transcript.", "citations_count": 4, "citation_yts": ["dxVcMDI7vyI"], "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dxVcMDI7vyI&t=887", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dxVcMDI7vyI&t=976", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dxVcMDI7vyI&t=708", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dxVcMDI7vyI&t=1240"], "citation_sources": ["S1", "S3", "S4", "S5"], "citations_valid": 1, "video_aligned": 1}
